My crontab (in /var/spool/cron/crontabs) entries were accidentally =
damaged
on my system.
The way to recover it is simple :=20
Normally, the .proto.. file becomes the standard file (without the
".proto.." prefix) during an installation.  You got a file for the user
root, adm and sys.
So, if you accidentally empty or delete the live copy,
you can often use the .proto.. version to figure out what used to be in
the file, as well as finding out what local changes have been made.
Thank you to all those who helped me solve my issue.

