From tru64-unix-managers  Mon Apr 23 14:36:07 2001
From: Stan Horwitz <stan () temple ! edu>
Date: Mon, 23 Apr 2001 14:36:07 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [Summary]: Problem with console manager software
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653646721654

Thanks to Paul LaMadeleine, Steve Smith, and Stuart Hayes. You each helped
get me to the solution. What I did was shut down consoled again. I
restarted the lat daemon. I also checked and saw that even after I
shutdown consoled, that a child process was still going. I killed that
process manually.  I then issued the "/sbin/console_start clean" again.
When I tried to make another connection with the "console" command, it
gave me the same error that the system was unavailable, but then the
display quickly switched to a message indicating that the console is now
available. I then checked the other console ports and they all work fine
now so our Console manager is fixed.


