The Question was :

Can we delete without problems all the files which are in the directory
/usr/var/adm/syslog.dated on a 4.0D true 64 ??=20

Thanks in advance.=20

Sophie AUBERTIER=20


My problem was that the cron entry to remove automatically the oldest
syslog.dated directories was no longer on my system.

I put the command

40 4 * * * find /var/adm/syslog.dated -depth -type d -ctime +5 -exec rm =
-rf
{} \;

to my cron root entry to solve the problem.

Thank you to all who replied !!

Sophie AUBERTIER

=20

