Thanks much to Pete Lindsay.
User marc showing up on file creations was not due to
tcb db, but rather old passwd.pag file.
ran mkpasswd, marc is now gone.

This is what Pete had to say:

If I am not mistaken tcb filesystem is the addition of
acls, while acls 
can
speficy the "default directory" acl they cannot
speficy a "default 
owner"
the only thing that sets owner ship is a process and
the only place 
that
ownership evalutated is the password database , notice
I didn't say
/etc/passwd.  This is because if your running Enhanced
Security or NIS  
or
have done a passwd hash, then you maybe looking
elsewhere for your user
name.  If one of these is the case we need to start
looking at other 
name
sources.



