Subject: SUMMARY: 4.0F sysman -clone equivelant
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=98686450511047

Thank you Paul Henderson...

Question:

sysman -clone -save works great on V5.0 to save network
configuration information.

Is there an equivelant command to create a config.cdf on 4.0F?

Pauls Answer:

Base OS installation cloning is available from 4.0 onward.

Common system configuration cloning (network, printers, routing, DNS,
NFS, etc etc) was added in 5.0. A config.cdf file is not supported in
4.0F.

