From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Apr 06 06:54:22 2001
From: Hannes Visagie <visagi_h () mtn ! co ! ug>
Date: Fri, 06 Apr 2001 06:54:22 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: How to verify disks write cache is switched off in fibre HSG80
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=98654021306272

Hi all

I need to verify that all the drives in a Fibre HSG80 write cache is
disabled {Write through}.  In case of power failure, cache on HSG80 is
battery backed up, but actual disks are not.  So there can be a potential
loss of data in extreme cases.

On normal SCSI controllers, this is usually easy to determine.  Use some
SCSI command and switch on/off.

Please note that this is for the actual disks, not configured RAID, LUN's.

AFAIK Compaq drives are default write cache off.

Thanks

