To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: RA8000, HSG + switch and 4.0F:  can it boot ??
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=98620598325826

Hello Managers,

I'd like to thank Eskil Swahn, Pat Barrowclough, Corinne Haesaerts, Alan
Davis, Alan, Bill Kirk, Dan Harrington, Matthias Dolder, Dennis Sylvester,
Pat O'Brien, Gert-Jan Hilbrands, Justin Richardson for their answers. 

I seems that:
- 4.0F can only be used with data disks but won't boot from this
configuration (you have to use a local system disk to boot)
- 4.0F needs the correct emx driver and firmware to function
- The disadvantage of a 4.0-F system is that it doesn't support the
alternative pathing mechanism as a v5.x system does
- Also, 4.0F has limits on the number of targets/bus (8) it supports. 

So i'll go for 5.1 SP2

Maurice


